# Bassidi Koné - Mali, West Africa

Want to know more about these fabulous artists we are hosting for Camp Afro Foli Drum & Dance Retreat? [Bassidi Koné](http://bassidikone.com/) is of Bwa ethnicity from the Segou region in Mali. Born into a Griot family, Bassidi grew up beside his father’s instrument, the [balafon](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e_nXGhpodYk) (a traditional, wooden xylophone), instilling in him his forefather’s traditional village songs and rhythms. Bassidi carried on his family’s musical heritage, showing promising skill in both the balafon and the djembe. [![Bassidi Kone](/media/2017/05/IMG_0786.jpg)](/bassidi-kone-mali-west-africa/img_0786/) After moving to Bamako at thirteen, Bassidi met Koninba Bagayogo, a meeting that profoundly influenced his musical career as a percussionist. Playing alongside this master djembe player, the young Bassidi extended his knowledge and skill, distinguishing himself through his innovative [solo lead playing](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_Xxs0r8eO4U) and technical virtuosity. Driven to defend his rich Bwa heritage, Bassidi Kone formed and now leads his multi-instrumental percussion and dance troupe, [Bwazan](http://bwazan-mali.com/) (_Bobo children)_, a family group from the same line of Griots. Bwazan are ambassadors of their musical heritage, promoting a message of peace, freedom, humility, and solidarity. Bassidi Kone will be teaching West African drumming on djembe and dundun at [Camp Afro Foli](/camp-afro-foli-drum-dance-retreat/) Drum & Dance Retreat. You can [Book Now](/product/camp-afro-foli-drum-dance-retreat/) for camp and grab the early bird special.
